{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106096","id":2499251732,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6U944U","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106096.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106096/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106096/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106096/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e3ce08e64fa5df523925deee1ef411f98b760e20","number":106096,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Roslyn Analyzer and Code Fix for repeated StringName implicit allocations","user":{"login":"myblindy","id":541998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTk5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy","html_url":"https://github.com/myblindy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myblindy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implicit `StringName` allocations from `string`s are fine, however they can hide the allocations from the user. This is even more important when they get repeatedly called in tight loops(*). Related issues: #106066 and #105750\r\n\r\nThis analyzer issues a warning when these constant `StringName` allocations happen in any kind of loop:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83148d41-c3a0-4bf3-b276-43f364081542)\r\n\r\nNote that only constant strings (as the compiler sees them, so it includes constant string concatenation, etc) are considered, something like this is still fine:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85c43c70-fe2d-453f-8213-5161e20adf8e)\r\n\r\nIt will offer to automatically fix it by creating a `static readonly StringName` field in the class and replace all allocations with it:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2407f118-9e13-4a52-85d5-79a0f46a4e8a)\r\n\r\nIt will also automatically reuse an existing such field, if one exists:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4142a666-0ad9-4b55-8bf7-c1ef25e9cd17)\r\n\r\n**(*) Note**: right now it only considers actual C# loops, it does not consider implicit frame loops like the ready or process functions. It would be easy to add if it's needed, however that would flag every single `StringName` implicit conversion like in input checks. There would be a performance gain from it, but.. it makes the Godot API look kind of shaky if it's needed to such a high degree.\r\n\r\n**Also note**: This is fully compatible with the #106066 proposal, as it checks the semantic model for implicit conversions. So if a `string` overload is present and the compiler successfully binds the `string` to it there will be no implicit conversion to trigger the analyzer:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/067d57d6-d8ea-4d3f-a47a-a4c18946fe51) vs ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/020499d3-1c39-4e41-91f7-3e85874ab145)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://a